  "response": "Based on the provided vulnerability description and constraints, I will assess the CVSS v3.1 base metric.\n\n**Attack Vector (AV):**\nThe vulnerability description mentions that an app may be able to access information about a user's contacts. This suggests that the attack vector is **Network (N)**, as the attacker would need to interact with the app remotely to exploit this issue.\n\n**Attack Complexity (AC):**\nThe complexity of the attack is considered **Low (L)**, as the attacker only needs to create an app that can access a user's contacts. This does not require significant expertise or resources.\n\n**Privileges Required (PR):**\nNo privileges are required for the attacker to exploit this issue, so the value is set to **None (N)**.\n\n**User Interaction (UI):**\nThe vulnerability description implies that some level of user interaction is required, as an app needs to be installed and interacted with by a user. Therefore, the value is set to **Required (R)**.\n\n**Scope (S):**\nThe scope of this issue is limited to the affected app and its users, so the value is set to **User (U)**.\n\n**Confidentiality Impact (C):**\nThe vulnerability allows an app to access information about a user's contacts. This could lead to unauthorized access to sensitive data, so the impact is considered **Low (L)**.\n\n**Integrity Impact (I):**\nThere is no indication that this issue affects the integrity of the system or data, so the impact is set to **None (N)**.\n\n**Availability Impact (A):**\nThe availability of the affected app and its services is not directly impacted by this vulnerability, so the impact is considered **None (N)**.\n\nUsing these metrics, I will calculate the CVSS v3.1 base score:\n\n**Vector String:**\nCVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N\n\n**Base Score:**\nBased on the calculated vector string, the base score is **4.0**.\n\nHere is the output in JSON format:\n```json\n{\n  \"attack_vector\": \"N\",\n  \"attack_complexity\": \"L\",\n  \"